<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <Itf Name="IResourceManager" Id="{ff689dff-7188-4d66-aad5-7e13264eb7c0}">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*!
<summary>Provides cyclic acquisition and release of a resource.</summary>
<description>
Call StartAcquire or StartRelease once, then drive the operation through IExecutable.Execute.
ResourceAcquired=TRUE completes acquisition; FALSE completes the release attempt.
One caller controls the manager at a time. Do not overlap operations or change configuration
while an operation is pending. Execute without a pending operation does nothing.
Cancellation of pending acquisition follows the concrete manager contract before release begins.
</description>
*)

INTERFACE IResourceManager EXTENDS IExecutable]]></Declaration>
    <Method Name="StartAcquire" Id="{34a23abc-a00b-434c-bab7-3d2d2c4d5b80}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[(*!
<summary>Requests resource acquisition once; Execute advances it.</summary>
<description>
Configure the manager before this call. Do not repeat the request while acquisition is pending.
Continue calling Execute until ResourceAcquired=TRUE or an exception is raised.
When already acquired, the existing resource is retained.
</description>
*)
METHOD StartAcquire]]></Declaration>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="GetResource" Id="{836c1686-7dc2-4e21-a310-8732d4b298fb}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[(*!
<summary>Returns a borrowed resource object owned by this manager.</summary>
<description>
The caller must not delete the returned object. It may be obtained before acquisition
and retained while the manager remains alive, including across release and reacquisition.
The object remains valid after release, but its presence does not mean the resource is acquired.
Use the underlying resource only after successful acquisition and before release begins.
Do not reuse a handle saved from an earlier acquisition after release.
</description>
*)
METHOD GetResource : IObject]]></Declaration>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="StartRelease" Id="{2458387f-c09a-488e-803e-6fe5eb3b8486}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[(*!
<summary>Requests resource release once; Execute advances it.</summary>
<description>
Call after acquisition has finished, including any cancellation-specific completion.
Do not repeat the request while release is pending. Continue calling Execute while
ResourceAcquired=TRUE; FALSE completes the cleanup attempt. Releasing an absent resource is allowed.
An exception from StartRelease or Execute is terminal for the task's release attempt: Task stops with
FinalStopReason=FAILURE and does not automatically retry this release.
Handle recoverable errors inside the manager if release should continue.
Define recovery for any resource still held after a terminal exception.
A best-effort manager may log a close error and finish its cleanup attempt
without throwing; physical release is not guaranteed by task termination.
</description>
*)

METHOD StartRelease]]></Declaration>
    </Method>
    <Property Name="ResourceAcquired" Id="{2052278d-b643-4655-a4d6-4cc5c02f2fea}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[PROPERTY ResourceAcquired : BOOL]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{6416f789-ba6f-4e49-b36c-9ec7c41d24fd}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[]]></Declaration>
      </Get>
    </Property>
  </Itf>
</TcPlcObject>